# Limits clasp push / watch to the files Apps Script needs.
#
# Why an allow-list (measured 2026-09-17, clasp 3.3.0):
# - A .claspignore **replaces** clasp's default ignore list (DEFAULT_CLASP_IGNORE).
#   A deny-list of just docs/** and test/** would therefore push files the default
#   used to skip, such as node_modules/**/*.js and anything that is not *.{gs,js,html}
#   (measured: node_modules/micromatch/index.js and .eslintrc.js became Tracked).
# - "Ignore everything, then allow what is needed" cannot grow the push set when
#   new files appear later.
#
# Measured with this file in place: clasp status tracks only
#   appsscript.json and Code.js (the ~1.45MB of HTML under docs/ is not uploaded).
#
# Note: clasp matches with dot: true, so `!*.js` also matches dotfiles such as
#   .eslintrc.js. The final `.*` undoes that (order matters). `*` does not cross
#   `/`, so only files at the repository root are included.
#
# When you add a GAS file, add a line to the allow-list below
# (if you forget, it shows up under "Untracked files" in clasp status).
**/**
!appsscript.json
!*.gs
!*.js
!*.html
.*
